<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35612" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-terrĕo</span></b> , ui, ĭtum,
			2, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to frighten</i> or <i>terrify
				thoroughly</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Eun. 5, 3, 13</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alios magnitudine poenarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes. B.
					G. 7, 4</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">50</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">metu perterriti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Caecin. 10, 26</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">obstupefactus ac perterritus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Cat. 2, 7, 14</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">maleficii conscientiā perterritus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Clu. 13, 38</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ossa mea perterrita sunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Job, 4, 14</span></i>
			 (but the true read., <i><span class="en">Cic. Caecin. 13, 37</span></i>, is
			proterritus).</div>
